<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andriandahifotsy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1685</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andriandahifotsy was a king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a> in the second half of the seventeenth century, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maroserana-dynasty">Maroserana dynasty</a>. Remembered as a great conqueror, he used firearms acquired from European traders to defeat neighbouring rulers and built up the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menabe">Menabe</a>. After his death around 1685 his sons founded further Sakalava realms, including Boina in the north-west.</p></div>
